    "body": "[Our `scandir()` function](https://github.com/pytest-dev/pytest/blob/24e84f08f43216f95620135305cbebe9f646e433/src/_pytest/pathlib.py#L950-L972) crashes if the directory to scan does not exist, which can happen if e.g. a tempory directory is deleted during collection (as in https://github.com/HypothesisWorks/hypothesis/issues/4200).  I therefore propose catching the directory-not-found error and returning `[]` in this case:\r\n\r\n```python\r\ntry:\r\n    with os.scandir(path) as s:\r\n        scanned = list(s)\r\nexcept FileNotFoundError:\r\n    return []\r\n# Skip entries with symlink loops and other brokenness, so the caller\r\n# doesn't have to deal with it.\r\nfor entry in scanned:\r\n    ...\r\n```",
